WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
- My next guest is a
talented comedian and actress

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:03.627
whose new book,

00:00:03.627 --> 00:00:06.130
"Very Fat, Very Brave" is out right now.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.210
She should add very funny
to the title 'cause she is,

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.043
and I love her.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.270
I'm talking about Nicole Byer, everybody.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.730
Hey, what's up, Nicole?

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.070
- Hi, how are you?

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:15.903
- I am so good.

00:00:15.903 --> 00:00:17.430
Oh my gosh, I love the flowers,

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.410
I love the whole vibe behind you!

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:20.243
- Thank you.

00:00:20.243 --> 00:00:24.330
My roommate, John Millhiser,
who's also a comedian.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.620
He did this all while
I was doing my makeup.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.910
- Oh my gosh, he's so good.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:30.050
Like an interior designer.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:30.883
That's so cool.

00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:33.110
I love your hair by the way, too.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:33.943
- Thank you!

00:00:33.943 --> 00:00:34.776
- That's so beautiful!

00:00:34.776 --> 00:00:36.700
Yeah, you've been out on the front lines

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.220
at protests recently.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.950
Has that experience given you hope,

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.890
or has it kind of deterred you?

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.550
I feel like I know several
people that have gone,

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.160
and there've been different
kinds of protests,

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.920
and different happenings in each one.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.870
So, what has your experience been like?

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.370
- It makes me feel hopeful
personally, because,

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.070
the protests have not stopped since May,

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.470
and we're now in June,

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:02.150
and I don't see them
slowing down or stopping.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.130
- Is there any particular moment

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.880
that has really stood out for you?

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.830
Since May and now we're moving into June?

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.350
- No particular moments.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.450
I mean, it's just really
depressing to wake up,

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.390
open Twitter and go, oh, okay.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:16.520
Somebody else's dead.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.353
- Yeah.

00:01:17.353 --> 00:01:19.310
- And, I don't know if things
will go back to normal.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:21.510
I mean, at least not for black people.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.480
We talk about it ad nauseum.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.010
I talk about it in my standup.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:28.660
So I don't know if there is a going back.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.863
If you're not radicalized for forever,

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.250
you're part of the problem.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.600
And I encourage a lot of white people

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:35.900
to read "White Fragility".

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.300
It is a wonderful book
that truly breaks down

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.320
why white people don't
wanna talk about race

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.620
and why their discomfort seems to

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:47.560
take precedent over learning.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:50.930
- And why, I think a lot of
people don't even notice it.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:51.780
They don't see it.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:52.640
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.306
- Oh yeah.
- It's like, if you're in it,

00:01:54.306 --> 00:01:55.972
you don't even see it a
lot sometimes. And it's --

00:01:55.972 --> 00:01:56.805
- Oh yeah, absolutely.

00:01:56.805 --> 00:01:57.860
- Not until you listen
and have conversations

00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:59.460
to where you see the difference,

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:00.870
and you hear the difference,

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.810
that you actually go, hmm, okay.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.070
I think that's a big problem
about it too, is the ignorance.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:08.170
I think educating oneself is probably

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.710
the most important thing
you can do right now.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.000
Other than listening.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.070
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.573
- Well, I don't even know how
to switch subjects on that.

00:02:16.573 --> 00:02:18.670
(laughing) But I'm going to
try and get a little lighter.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:21.160
So we're not supposed to,
there's no segue, Nicole,

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.980
I'm not that clever.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.240
But I do wanna talk about it

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.930
'cause I know you protested
during the quarantine.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.263
But, we've all been doing
completely different things.

00:02:29.263 --> 00:02:31.830
that maybe we would've
ever done beforehand too,

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.663
just to stay sane.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.180
Because on top of
everything that's going on,

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.350
there's just a lot of emotional

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:38.570
roller coaster stuff happening.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:41.730
And, for me, I've started doing things

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:42.950
that I never did before,

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:43.920
or like things with my kids

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.580
that I never did before I had time for.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:48.110
Is there anything that you've
been doing during quarantine

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.710
that you never did before that
you're like, sure, why not?

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:53.691
- Well, when I was a kid,
I remember rollerskating,

00:02:53.691 --> 00:02:54.524
but I don't remember like roller skating.

00:02:57.281 --> 00:02:58.199
So I was like,

00:02:58.199 --> 00:02:59.032
(laughing)

00:02:59.032 --> 00:03:01.080
I wanna learn how to roller skate.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.920
So I've been learning how to roller skate.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.070
- That's amazing!

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:04.903
- What?

00:03:04.903 --> 00:03:05.736
- That's amazing!

00:03:05.736 --> 00:03:07.240
- Oh, thank you!

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.284
I skinned my knee two days ago.

00:03:09.284 --> 00:03:11.230
(laughing)

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:13.740
Because I almost crashed into a Mercedes.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:16.724
And I was like, God forbid a person has --

00:03:16.724 --> 00:03:18.912
- I'm gonna take my knee
out before that car.

00:03:18.912 --> 00:03:19.900
(laughing)

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.650
And then I also I've been pole dancing.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.600
But I've been doing that --
- That's hard!

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.910
- Yeah, it's so hard.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.660
I did this class on
Sunday and I'm so sore,

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:30.610
but it like --

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:31.443
- [Kelly] I can't,

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:32.410
I'm too heavy for that.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.084
Like I can't hold myself up.

00:03:34.084 --> 00:03:36.680
- I'm much bigger than you and I can.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:39.466
- I'm just telling you from my experience,

00:03:39.466 --> 00:03:43.015
I literally was like, nah, this
fine behind ain't for this.

00:03:43.015 --> 00:03:43.848
(laughing)

00:03:43.848 --> 00:03:44.681
I know.

00:03:44.681 --> 00:03:45.514
(laughing)

00:03:45.514 --> 00:03:48.300
- It's hard that if you can
do that, you are incredible.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.131
- It's so hard.

00:03:50.131 --> 00:03:51.797
- Yeah.
- And I love it so much,

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:53.557
'cause it's like a tangible
thing where you're like,

00:03:53.557 --> 00:03:55.903
oh, I couldn't do this yesterday,
but now I can do it today.

00:03:55.903 --> 00:03:57.450
- Yeah, and it makes you feel sexy.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.130
It's like working out and it
makes you feel like a little,

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.180
well, I imagine it makes you feel sexy

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.740
when you're doing it well.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.404
I wouldn't know, firsthand.

00:04:04.404 --> 00:04:05.490
- I wouldn't know either.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:07.113
I'm very mediocre.

00:04:09.858 --> 00:04:11.500
- Maybe it's 'cause I was
drinking the time I tried it,

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.573
but I, yeah, I was not good.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.450
But Nicole, I love your book too.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:17.860
Okay, I have your book here actually,

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:18.900
'cause I love it.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.340
I think it's amazing because

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.500
that's one thing I love about you

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.630
is that you're so honest
and in a funny way.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.320
You're like this isn't, I mean,

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.010
so your book is called
"Very Fat, Very Brave".

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:31.840
And I think I'm kind of aware
of where the title comes from

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:32.980
because I'm a fan of yours,

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:35.120
but for everybody that doesn't know,

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.140
why did you title it that?

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:41.180
- So, when a fat woman
posts on the internet,

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.120
a picture of themselves in a bikini,

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:46.140
or something revealing, the internet goes,

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.610
my God, you're so brave!

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:52.070
Which is the fully insane thing,

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:54.090
to be like, somebody who's wearing

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.880
a bathing suit to go swimming is brave?

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.960
No, they're just wearing
the correct article

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.510
of clothing to do an activity.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:01.080
- Well, and it's almost insulting,

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:01.913
'cause it's like --

00:05:01.913 --> 00:05:02.790
- Oh, it's fully insulting.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:03.750
- I always love that, and they're like,

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.140
Oh, you're so confident.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.120
You just don't care.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.667
And I'm like, what?

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.146
(laughing)

00:05:09.146 --> 00:05:09.979
- You don't care?

00:05:09.979 --> 00:05:12.754
'Cause I'm like, I spent hours trying --

00:05:12.754 --> 00:05:14.910
- And like, I care about things.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:17.160
Maybe just not things
that you find important.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:20.060
But I was like, let's not
write me off like that.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.510
Yeah, it's funny how they they're like,

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:22.343
Oh, you're so confident.

00:05:22.343 --> 00:05:23.340
I'm like, I'm not confident.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.630
I'm just being.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.870
- Yes, yes.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:28.230
It's so frustrating.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:29.800
So it's very tongue-in-cheek.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.980
I don't think I'm actually brave,

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.430
but I would love to meet
somebody who is like.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.410
Oh, she actually thinks she's
brave for being in a bikini?

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:40.250
I want to meet that
person to be like, really?

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:41.600
- I wanna have coffee with that person.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.433
(laughing)

00:05:42.433 --> 00:05:45.540
Well, in the book you have a
way of dealing with haters.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.600
And I want you to tell
everybody what that is.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:50.003
- Oh, I have so many different ways.

00:05:52.496 --> 00:05:54.644
- I have a particular
favorite, but, you go ahead.

00:05:54.644 --> 00:05:56.400
- Wait, which one is your favorite?

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.800
- I like, whenever you say that,

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.260
'cause this is my thing I always say,

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:01.460
I think that's why I relate to it.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.130
I'm like, do you have that much time

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.503
to sit at home and rail on me right now?

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.460
I don't even know you.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:10.813
You could have just ignored it.

00:06:10.813 --> 00:06:11.790
It's like,

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.360
look, I want your life.
- Yes.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:14.780
- If you have that kind of time.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:15.613
You turn around and go,

00:06:15.613 --> 00:06:16.930
I'm sorry your life is so little

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.200
that you're worried about me over here?

00:06:20.864 --> 00:06:21.697
I love that.
- Yeah.

00:06:21.697 --> 00:06:22.910
I like that one too.

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:26.740
Another one I have is if
someone calls you a cow,

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.622
you just turn around and moo at them.

00:06:28.622 --> 00:06:30.872
(laughing)

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:33.100
- I love that!

